Z||000000||gtsonly||08-13-2000||04:29 AM||||i am getting a code 14, and i am sure it is the sensor going to the ecm. which sensor is it? you'all have told me it is the sensor by the thermostat with the yellow and black wires but i have no sensor with yellow and black wires. by the thermostat there is one sensor with one wire(green with a white strip) and there is one in front of that with a black and a red with a wite strip. is the sensor i need the later mentioned one? i am lost and i need to get rid of my night light on the dash (check engine light)!!!!!!<P> help,<BR>     chris hatch<BR>        1986.5 gt w/t-tops||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gokart||08-13-2000||06:13 AM||||Chris is right about these wires! He was over my place yesterday and we were going to change the sensor but the wires are not the colors stated on tech pages. We checked out mine and they are the same colors as his! There is no yellow and black wires leading to either sensor by thermo.<P>Marc 87GT||||reg||4
Z||000002||cobra427||08-14-2000||02:04 AM||||gtsonly,<BR>the sensor up by the thermastat is the fan switch. That has the green and white wire , the other sensor that has the wellow and black wires is the temperature sensor and that is located to the left of # 5cylinder. you will see a heatshield that protects it there. From what I see in the shop manual, that is the one that goes to the ECM.<P>There is a raft of things to test so if you need more info ,sing out<P>cobra||||reg||1
Z||000003||cobra427||08-14-2000||03:19 AM||||After further investigation, I see that I was incorrect. The coolant temp sensor by #5 cyl does not have the yellow and black wires.And I also noticed that the sensor in question must be the one that runs out of the lower intake manifold,in the center of,and just below the thermastat fill pipe(pointing horizontally to east side of car)and under the EGR solinoid. I could not confirm the color of the wires,but that is the only coolant sensor left. Next to the cooling fan switch(green and white wires),is the Thermo Time switch and thats not it. Thos both reside verticlally to the right of the fill pipe.<BR>   Sorry for the earlier misinfo.:^(||||reg||11
Z||000004||gtsonly||08-14-2000||08:27 AM||||dont worry about any misinfo!! this dumb sensor is kicking my a--! i will try the other one. there are only three correct and of those three only one goes to the ecm?? two of the sensors i see have just the one wire which is green with white the other one has two wires, one black and one red with a white strip. i will try that!!<P>  chris hatch||||reg||14
Z||000005||tgowens||08-14-2000||01:57 PM||||chris, cobra427 is correct on the location of the coolant temp sensor but it is hard to see from the top -- as you stand on the passenger side of the car, look down and behind the coolant thermostat -- believe me, it's there but really hard to see -- there ARE two wires (and I have forgotten the colors now) in an oval shaped "boot" plugging into the sensor -- mine was cracked and allowed water to get in and short it and it caused the code plus the idiot light -- the sensors can be obtained from Napa or other large auto parts store. keep looking in that area and you will see it -- if you stick your arm down behind the thermostat, it will be about 10" to 12" below the top of the thermostat cap......hope this helps......||||reg||1
